{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509787-malleus-maleficarum-and-monster-s-confessions","id":509787,"title":"Malleus Maleficarum and monster's confessions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-10T05:12:34-07:00","id":509787,"title":"Malleus Maleficarum and monster's confessions","content":"I preper <b>Mage</b> game in that my PCs wizards will be hunt by <i>Hammer on </i><i>Witches</i>. In <b>Compact &amp; Conspiracies</b> there is mentioned that <i>Malleus</i> is always looking for final confession of the monster they get - and counts on it's redemption. With vampires or werewolves there is not big problem on this - if they are low on Vitea or Essence, they cannot fight it more and maybe question ( and tortured ) in peace by Inquisitor. Monsters will still hold conciseness enough to answer &quot;truthfully&quot; questions, but being largely defenseless, especially when using Banes of Fire or Silver for that.<br /> <br /> But Awakened mages can <b>always</b> cast spell. The only possibility is there they are so half-concussions they cannot think straight. And in this condition, they &quot;confessions&quot; are unreliable - when you question someone that cannot collect his thoughts, you cannot be sure of his words. <b>So how would <i>Malleus </i>solve this problem, when witches are so central to it's war with servants of Satan?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T18:39:14-07:00","id":510302,"title":"","content":"I think the best way is to restrain the Mage and use whatever anti-magic benedictions they might have on hand. Also, in that case, the Malleus are smart enough to realize that confessions gained via torture are, at best, not reliable information at all. They've been at this for <i>centuries</i>, they probably know more about torture than the CIA does about waterboarding. One of the best ways to describe what I imagine are the &quot;techniques&quot; of the Malleus is honestly <a href=\"http://www.doctorshrugs.com/foxhound/comic.php?id=497\" target=\"_blank\">this comic.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T19:01:28-07:00","id":510308,"title":"","content":"The first thought that honestly pops to mind to me is death's bed confessions. The Malleus focuses on mortally wounding a witch and then tries to get them to make a confession/renounciation before they bleed out. That, or else they are willing to &quot;bend the rules&quot; a little - keep in mind that the MM is willing to break a LOT of Catholic rules, including the sarosanctity of the confessional, in their crusade.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Benedictions; use the powers of god to counteract the satantic workings of witches to counter them. Holy relics and stuff like that which disrupt magical powers.<br /> <br /> That said... I honestly don't think that the Malleus succeeds in hunting down Awakened too often, or at least catching them and forcing a confession. Most of the &quot;witches&quot; it gets are probably lesser templates or humans using the lower-tier Dread Powers version of spells from Witch Finder. As you've pointed out, Awakened are hard to hold without killing them, and, let's face it: if I knew the people around me were the Inquisition Reborn? And that I had nothing to look forward to either way? You can bet your ass I would try the biggest, nastiest spells I can think of; even if the Backlash kills me, I can hope that the Paradox will take them with me. I'd rather get sucked out of reality and leave some howling blasphemy against reality in my place than be tortured to death for &quot;the sake of my soul&quot;, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T13:08:23-07:00","id":511064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509787-malleus-maleficarum-and-monster-s-confessions?p=510308#post510308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thought that honestly pops to mind to me is death's bed confessions. The Malleus focuses on mortally wounding a witch and then tries to get them to make a confession/renounciation before they bleed out. That, or else they are willing to &quot;bend the rules&quot; a little - keep in mind that the MM is willing to break a LOT of Catholic rules, including the sarosanctity of the confessional, in their crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>This idea I like very much. I would only add to this idea of &quot;curing&quot; mortal wounds by the nun with Benedictions - and repeate the torture process. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509787-malleus-maleficarum-and-monster-s-confessions?p=510308#post510308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, Benedictions; use the powers of god to counteract the satantic workings of witches to counter them. Holy relics and stuff like that which disrupt magical powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought today about it on the bus. As I see it - there is not <b>anything</b> like this in the <b>Witch Finders </b>or any other book in <b>Hunter </b>line. That is very odd, as Counterspell is only 3 dot on Prime and most of effects like these are somehow doable by Hunters Endowments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509787-malleus-maleficarum-and-monster-s-confessions?p=510308#post510308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said... I honestly don't think that the Malleus succeeds in hunting down Awakened too often, or at least catching them and forcing a confession. Most of the &quot;witches&quot; it gets are probably lesser templates or humans using the lower-tier Dread Powers version of spells from Witch Finder. As you've pointed out, Awakened are hard to hold without killing them, and, let's face it: if I knew the people around me were the Inquisition Reborn? And that I had nothing to look forward to either way? You can bet your ass I would try the biggest, nastiest spells I can think of; even if the Backlash kills me, I can hope that the Paradox will take them with me. I'd rather get sucked out of reality and leave some howling blasphemy against reality in my place than be tortured to death for &quot;the sake of my soul&quot;, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>That why vampires are first priority for Malleus Enemies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-11-2015, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}